# HP40gs stock launch through the original APLET UI and serial disk.
# HP40gs boots into the CAS front end more slowly than HP39gs, then follows the
# same host-completion-gated lazy-fetch path.
2000 tap f6
4000 tap f6
13000 tap home
15000 tap aplet
16000 capture aplet-library
17000 tap f5
18000 capture receive-menu

# HP40gs 2.22 RECEIVE FROM order has no HP39 (IrDA) entry:
#   HP39/40 (USB), HP39/40 (Ser), USB Disk drive, Ser. Disk drive.
18500 tap down
19200 tap down
19900 tap down
20200 capture receive-serial-disk
20600 tap enter

40000 capture remote-aplet
41500 tap enter
43000 capture lazy-fetch
44000 host-gate

# Times below are relative to host-gate release, not emulator start. Kermit EOF
# proves the bytes have arrived, but Stock can still be committing the fetched
# aplet/library or unwinding the serial-disk UI. Retry ENTER sparsely instead
# of guessing a fixed post-transfer delay. Once HPC1 reaches KBRD the harness
# suppresses later sequence key-downs, so these retries cannot contaminate the
# strict payload keyboard progression.
0 monitor 90000
500 capture fetch-complete
1000 tap enter
11000 tap enter
21000 tap enter
31000 tap enter
46000 tap enter
61000 tap enter
